SUMMARY:Neutron-distribution radius from higher moments of nuclear charge d
 istribution
DESCRIPTION:The nuclear charge density distribution\, $\\rho(r)$\, determin
 ed by elastic electron scattering\, provides essential information on nucl
 ear structure. Its moments\, $<r_c^n>=\\frac{1}{Z}\\int r^n \\rho_c(r) d^3
 r$ (Z:atomic number) are also important observables\; in particular\, the 
 fourth moment\, $<r_c^4>$\, has recently attracted attention because of it
 s close relation to the neutron distribution radius [\nhttps://indico.ijcl
 ab.in2p3.fr/event/14306/
LOCATION:IJCLab
URL:https://indico.ijclab.in2p3.fr/event/14306/
